iform(size:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph\/isuniform(size:)","title":"isUniform(size:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether every hyperedge has exactly "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"type":"text","text":" members (Berge’s k-uniform). Singletons and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty hyperedges count (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_uniform"},{"type":"text","text":" ignores singletons); vacuously true with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges. O(m)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isUniform"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"size"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/isUniform(size:)"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/cliqueExpansion()":{"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph\/cliqueexpansion()","title":"cliqueExpansion()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clique expansion (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", Berge’s 2-section): every vertex, isolated ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, in vertex-index order, and an edge between every two vertices that share a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge, once, with no self-loops. Edges ascend by (index of u, index of v), u the lower."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Singletons and empty hyperedges add no edge. Lossy and quadratic: one hyperedge of k members"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is k(k − 1)\/2 edges."}],"role":"symbol","